---
const stages = [
  {
    label: 'Hardware audio capture',
    detail: 'Sample microphone input in the browser / client environment.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Buffered chunk processing',
    detail: 'Accumulate audio until enough samples are ready for neural inference.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Transcript confidence filtering',
    detail: 'Suppress low-confidence segments before they enter the caption queue.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Fluid UI compositing',
    detail: 'Render animated overlay graphics without unnecessary layout churn or visible jitter.',
  },
];
---

<figure class="speech-pipeline not-prose">
  <header>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Live speech interface</p>
      <h3>Four operational domains coordinate continuously.</h3>
      <p class="dek">The interface spans capture, buffering, transcription policy, and rendering rather than treating speech-to-text as one isolated model call.</p>
    </div>
    <span class="badge">On-device pipeline</span>
  </header>

  <ol class="stages" aria-label="speechBubbles operational domains">
    {stages.map((stage, index) => (
      <li>
        <span class="index">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
        <strong>{stage.label}</strong>
        <p>{stage.detail}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <figcaption>
    The current public backend uses fixed-duration buffering and direct Whisper transcription. PyAnnote VAD scaffolding exists in the repository but is not active in the current <code>process_buffer()</code> path.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .speech-pipeline {
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 0.7rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
  }

  .speech-pipeline :global(p),
  .speech-pipeline :global(h3),
  .speech-pipeline :global(ol),
  .speech-pipeline :global(li) { margin: 0; }

  .speech-pipeline :global(ol) { padding: 0; list-style: none; }

  header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .badge,
  .index {
    font-family: var(--font-mono-ui);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.54rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
  }

  h3 {
    margin-top: 0.45rem !important;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.55rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.16;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .dek {
    margin-top: 0.45rem !important;
    max-width: 46rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .badge {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.47rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }

  .stages {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .stages li {
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    padding: 2.7rem 1rem 1.1rem;
  }

  .index {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.95rem;
    left: 1rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }

  .stages strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .stages p {
    margin-top: 0.45rem !important;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.67rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  figcaption {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  figcaption :global(code) {
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-family: var(--font-mono-ui);
    font-size: inherit;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .stages { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    header { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.75rem; }
  }
</style>